      "excerpt": "Choosing between Flutter and React Native can make or break your mobile startup. We benchmark performance, native bridge overhead, rendering engines, and team velocity.",
      "content": "<h2>The Dilemma: Choosing the Right Framework</h2>\n<p>Building separate native apps for iOS and Android often doubles development costs and timelines. Cross-platform engineering has reached native parity, with Flutter and React Native dominating the market.</p>\n\n<h3>Flutter's Impeller Rendering Engine</h3>\n<p>Flutter compiles directly to native ARM machine code with its high-performance Impeller engine, ensuring smooth 120 FPS animations, complete widget customizability, and pixel perfection across all devices.</p>\n\n<h3>React Native with New Architecture & TurboModules</h3>\n<p>React Native's latest architecture eliminates the legacy asynchronous bridge, enabling direct C++ JSI communication and instant rendering speeds with the vast JavaScript and React ecosystem.</p>\n\n<h2>Key Evaluation Criteria</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Development Speed:</strong> React Native wins if your team already excels in React & TypeScript.</li>\n  <li><strong>Visual Customization:</strong> Flutter excels when custom 2D canvas graphics and intricate transitions are paramount.</li>\n  <li><strong>Ecosystem & Libraries:</strong> Both offer battle-tested enterprise modules and robust community support.</li>\n</ul>",
